1. Task 4.4 — `harness/model-guide/quota.ts`

  The tool reads `GET /api/quota/<id>` of spec D15 for the four providers
  with a source. The base is `--base`, else `BENCH_QUOTA_BASE`, else the port
  of `openchamber status --json`. Every window below 70 % gives `ready`. A
  window of 70 % or more gives `wait`. A quota error, a limit error, a read
  failure, an empty window set, a missing `usedPercent`, a string value, and
  a value of `1e999` give `stopped` with one line `quota: <reason>` on
  stderr. A provider with no source gives `ready` and the cap 1 with no
  request. A provider with a source gives the cap 3. The read times out at
  5 s, and the whole answer is parsed, so a 2 MiB body with 200 windows
  works.

  Fix commit 82a0e6a: `void main()` replaces top-level await. The review
  runner copies the tool into a temp repo that holds no `type: module`
  package.json, and tsx then compiles the file as CJS.

2. Task 4.5 — `harness/model-guide/routes.json`

  The file holds the nine rows of spec D12 in order, each with exactly
  `family`, `route`, `kind`, `quota_provider`, and `quota_source`. The kinds
  are `plan` and `free` only. The Hy row `opencode/hy4-flash-free` is
  present. There is no second-judge row, because spec D11 keeps the fallback
  "no ready route". The file holds no test of its own, so the three Phase 4
  files prove it. All three pass at the 4.7 HEAD.

3. Task 4.6 — `harness/model-guide/provider-credential.sh`

  `seed <p>` reads the shared store with one `opencode auth export` call,
  retried on a transient failure with the waits of
  `BENCH_CREDENTIAL_SEED_DELAYS`, and imports the one active entry of the
  provider with `opencode auth import`. The payload goes over the pipe of
  the import call and never touches a disk. `scan-values <p>` prints the
  access value and the orgID of the entry, one per line. A provider with no
  entry gives exit 2 and one named line. A bad `AGENT_TIMEOUT` or a bad
  `BENCH_CREDENTIAL_SEED_DELAYS` gives exit 2 before any call.

4. Task 4.7 — `harness/model-guide/review-run.sh`

  The runner reads the quota before each pass and before each diff. A pass
  starts only on `ready`. It stops at a window of 80 % and leaves the pass
  `open`. A route with no quota source runs at most 1 pass per night. Each
  call is `run --standalone --format json --model <route>` with the job
  store of `opencode_host_run`, the job config that denies the eight tools,
  and the prompt on stdin. It retries a transport error twice, treats an
  empty answer as no response, and marks a Go route with the region error
  `region-blocked`. It scans each raw output before the store, and it
  deletes the output and stops the pass on a hit. A refusal prints one line
  `review-run: <check>` on stdout and exits 2 before any write.

  Blocked first, then repaired. The first run of `review-run.test.ts`
  reached `Tests  2 failed | 21 passed (23)`. Two Red cases could not pass
  under spec D12 to D15: R4 case 1 wrote its unknown route into the temp
  `routes.json`, and R6 case 2 read 79 % from the first quota read, which
  D15 and R5 make `wait`. Green did not edit the test. The Mid Red fix
  8e111d2 corrected both cases, and the file then gave `Tests  23 passed
  (23)`.

